 happen to the stream flow in the Yakima River Basin due to global warming?", "A": "It will decrease.", "S": "Decreased snowpack and earlier runoff will decrease stream flow."}, {"Q": "What is the goal of Seattle's Climate Action Plan?", "A": "To reduce greenhouse gases (GHG) by about 680,000 tons per year.", "S": "The end affect should be a reduction of greenhouse gases (GHG) by about 680,000 tons per year."}, {"Q": "What might happen to the area of distribution of marine resources due to climate change?", "A": "They will move towards the North or South pole, whichever is closest.", "S": "Climate change will also result in modifications of the area of distribution of marine resources. Most likely they will move towards the North or South pole, whichever is closest."}, {"Q": "What areas in Washington are at high risk for flooding?", "A": "Homes and businesses within reach of tidewater and low-lying agricultural areas in Washington are at high risks for flooding.", "S": "Homes and businesses within reach of tidewater and low-lying agricultural areas in Washington are at high risks for flooding."}, {"Q": "What are the effects of climate change on amphibians?", "A": "Amphibians stand to be some of the worst affected by climate change, due largely to the dependence on water regimes and need for specific microhabitats, as well as their limited dispersal abilities.", "S": "Amphibians stand to be some of the worst affected by climate change, due largely to the dependence on water regimes and need for specific microhabitats, as well as their limited dispersal abilities."}, {"Q": "What is the average result of the upfront cost of 2% to support green design?", "A": "Life cycle savings of 20% of total construction, more than ten times the initial investment costs.", "S": "An upfront cost of 2% to support green design would on average result in life cycle savings of 20% of total construction, more than ten times the initial investment costs."}, {"Q": "What is the reason for the decrease in milk production in Whatcom County?", "A": "The decrease in food availability during summer is due to increasing annual temperatures that shift precipitation levels and cause a faster run-off of snowpack.", "S": "The decrease in food availability during summer is due to increasing annual temperatures that shift precipitation levels and cause a faster run-off of snowpack."}, {"Q": "What is the estimated economic impact of restored salmon habitat on recreational fisheries in the state of Washington?", "A": "$1 billion in revenue and 9,400 jobs.", "S": "A 2003 report by the U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service and a 2001 report by the American Sportfishing Association estimates that the economic impact in 2001 of restored salmon habitat on recreational fisheries in the state of Washington could potentially have yielded $1 billion in revenue and 9,400 jobs."}, {"Q": "What is the main source of CO2 emissions in Washington State?", "A": "Human activities including burning fossil fuels, waste, and wood products.", "S": "Human activities including burning fossil fuels, waste, and wood products cause CO2 emissions."}, {"Q": "What is the main factor affecting the supply and demand of electricity in Washington State?", "A": "Annual temperature changes.", "S": "The biggest factors determining the effects on electricity are annual temperature changes and the change in peak snowpack melt and stream flow."}, {"Q": "What is the main source of greenhouse gas emissions?", "A": "Human activities including burning fossil fuels, waste, and wood products.", "S": "Human activities including burning fossil fuels, waste, and wood products cause CO2 emissions."}, {"Q": "What is the estimated cost of purchasing a license or vessel through Vessel Buyback Programs and License Retirement Programs?", "A": "The average cost is $10,000 for salmon and small vessel fleets, but can rise as high as $10 million for a factory trawler.", "S": "The average cost of a license or vessel purchased fewer th